{color.GG}Rmext {color.N}removes file extensions from matching files, with support for recursive directory traversal and extension filtering.

Usage: {color.GG}rmext {color.CC}<path> [--ext <.ext, ...>] [--no-recursive] [--exclude <syntax>|--exclude-list <lists.scfg>]{color.N}

Example:
    {color.R}- {color.GG}rmext {color.CC}~/.local/bin/ --ext '.js, .sh, .py, .rb'{color.N}
    {color.R}- {color.GG}rmext {color.CC}src/ --ext '.tmp'{color.N}
    {color.R}- {color.GG}rmext {color.CC}mydir/ --ext '.bak' --no-recursive{color.N}
    {color.R}- {color.GG}rmext {color.CC}mydir/ --exclude '"mylib" from "mydir/mytool"'{color.N}

Example {color.BB}.scfg {color.N}syntax:
{color.DG}// comment{color.N}
{color.YY}"myinternallib" {color.PP}from {color.YY}"lib/python/mytool"{color.N}
{color.YY}"include" {color.PP}from {color.YY}"bin/ctool"{color.N}